## 7. 🏢 Doosre Repo ka Self-Hosted Runner Apne Repo mein Kaise Use Karein?

Company environments mein aksar ek hi VM par runner chalta hai jise multiple repositories share karti hain.

### Case 1: Agar Runner Organization Level par hai (Best & Common)
* Runner poori GitHub Organization ke liye registered hota hai.
* **Aapko kya karna hai:** Apne GitHub Org Admin se bas itna bolna hai:
  > *"Mere naye repo (`terrafrom`) ko us existing **Runner Group** mein access add kar do."*
* Access milte hi aapke workflow mein `runs-on: self-hosted` likhte hi job automatically us VM par chali jayegi!

### Case 2: Agar Runner sirf kisi doosre Specific Repo mein registered hai
* Ek single runner application ek time par ek hi repo se register hota hai.
* **Solution 1 (Recommended):** Admin se bolein ki us runner ko Repo-level se hata kar **Organization level** par shift kar de taaki saari repos share kar sakein.
* **Solution 2:** Usi same VM par ek doosra folder bana kar (jaise `C:\actions-runner-repo2`) ek aur runner listener run karke aapke repo se connect kar diya jaye.

